IMPORT prelude

-- Agency for Science, Technology and Research Act 1990 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person or business that meets
-- A*STAR: the two offences (s 19 secrecy, s 20 the Agency's symbol), the bar on personal suits (s 17), the power to give financial
-- assistance (s 7(1)(d)), how a deed is executed (s 4(2)), the financial year (s 14), the metrology staff transferred in 2008
-- (s 23), and the Schedule rules on who may sit on the Agency and how it decides (s 5; Schedule paras 3, 9, 11, 13).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ASTRA1990.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its
-- metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026. The latest amending Act in the legislative history is Act 5
-- of 2018 (Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018, s 48, in force 1 April 2018).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0155 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is mostly constitutional (it sets up a statutory board), so SCOPED to the provisions an outsider,
-- a grant-seeker, a member or an employee actually meets. Not encoded: the functions (s 6, except as noted), most of the powers in
-- s 7(1), grants-in-aid, borrowing, shares, bank accounts and investment (ss 8-12), Ministerial directions (s 15), the chief
-- executive (s 16), the 2002 renaming saving (s 21), the 2008 transfer of property and contracts (ss 22, 24), discipline for
-- pre-transfer misconduct (s 25), and Schedule paras 1, 2, 4-8, 10, 12 and 14.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Agency for Science, Technology and Research Act 1990`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `19 -- preservation of secrecy`

-- s 19(1): "Except for the purpose of performing his or her duties or exercising his or her functions or when lawfully required
-- to do so by any court or where required or allowed by the provisions of any written law, a member, officer, employee or agent of
-- the Agency must not disclose any information relating to the affairs of any person which has been obtained by the member,
-- officer, employee or agent in the performance of his or her duties or the exercise of his or her functions."
-- (2): "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both."
DECLARE Disclosure HAS
    `made by a member, officer, employee or agent of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of information about a person's affairs obtained in the course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for the purpose of performing duties or functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lawfully required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required or allowed by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 19` IF
        `the disclosure`'s `made by a member, officer, employee or agent of the Agency`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `of information about a person's affairs obtained in the course of duties`
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `for the purpose of performing duties or functions`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `lawfully required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `the disclosure`'s `required or allowed by a written law`)

§§ `20 -- the Agency's symbol`

-- s 20(1): the Agency "has the exclusive right to the use of such symbol or representation as the Agency may select or devise".
-- (2): any person who (a) "uses a symbol or representation that is identical to the Agency's symbol or representation"; or (b)
-- uses one "that so resembles the Agency's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive
-- or cause confusion", is guilty of an offence: "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months
-- or to both". The text states no exception (for example for use with the Agency's consent) and no mental element.
DECLARE SymbolUse IS ONE OF
    `a symbol identical to the Agency's`
    `a symbol so like the Agency's as to be likely to confuse`
    `a symbol that resembles the Agency's but is unlikely to confuse`
    `an unrelated symbol`

GIVEN `the use` IS A SymbolUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 20` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `a symbol identical to the Agency's` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a symbol so like the Agency's as to be likely to confuse` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlawful disclosure under section 19`
    `misuse of the Agency's symbol under section 20`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure under section 19` THEN 2000
    WHEN `misuse of the Agency's symbol under section 20` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure under section 19` THEN 12
    WHEN `misuse of the Agency's symbol under section 20` THEN 6

§§ `17 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 17: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Agency or other
-- person acting under the direction of the Agency for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the execution
-- or purported execution of this Act." The Agency itself is not protected: s 3(1)(a) makes it capable of "suing and being sued".
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Agency`
    `an officer or employee of the Agency`
    `a person acting under the Agency's direction`
    `the Agency itself`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `done in execution or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suit is barred by section 17` IF
        `done in good faith`
    AND `done in execution or purported execution of the Act`
    AND CONSIDER `the defendant`
        WHEN `the Agency itself` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7(1)(d) -- financial assistance`

-- s 7(1)(d): the Agency MAY provide financial assistance (including scholarships) "(i) for the training and development of
-- manpower in Singapore required for or conducive to the conduct of scientific and technological research and development, or to
-- the commercial application of scientific knowledge or technology; or (ii) to any person in the public or private sector for
-- scientific and technological research and development, or for any commercial application of scientific knowledge or
-- technology, in areas defined by the Agency". s 2: "financial assistance" includes grant, loan, loan guarantee, bonds and equity.
-- This is a power, not an entitlement; s 6(4) says nothing in s 6 imposes "any form of duty or liability enforceable by
-- proceedings before any court".
DECLARE Assistance IS ONE OF
    `a scholarship to train a researcher in Singapore`
    `a grant to a company for research in an area the Agency has defined`
    `a loan to a company commercialising technology in an area the Agency has defined`
    `a grant to a company for research outside any area the Agency has defined`
    `a loan to a restaurant with no scientific or technological element`

GIVEN `the assistance` IS AN Assistance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assistance is within section 7(1)(d)` IF
    CONSIDER `the assistance`
    WHEN `a scholarship to train a researcher in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a grant to a company for research in an area the Agency has defined` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a loan to a company commercialising technology in an area the Agency has defined` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4(2) -- executing a deed`

-- s 4(2): deeds requiring the seal "must be sealed with the common seal of the Agency in the presence of, and be signed by -- (a)
-- the Chairperson or a Deputy Chairperson of the Agency; and (b) an employee of the Agency who is authorised by resolution or
-- otherwise in writing". (3): such signing is "sufficient evidence" the seal was duly affixed.
GIVEN `signed by the Chairperson or a Deputy Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by an employee authorised in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deed is executed under section 4(2)` IF
    `signed by the Chairperson or a Deputy Chairperson` AND `signed by an employee authorised in writing`

§§ `14 -- financial year`

-- s 14: "The financial year of the Agency begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the Agency's financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

§§ `23 -- metrology staff transferred on 1 January 2008`

-- s 23(1): every person employed immediately before 1 January 2008 by the Board (s 22(3): the Standards, Productivity and
-- Innovation Board) in its national metrology centre is transferred to the Agency "on terms no less favourable". (5): any term on
-- length of service "must recognise the length of service of the persons so transferred while in the employment of the Board to
-- be service with the Agency".
GIVEN `employed in the Board's national metrology centre immediately before 1 January 2008` IS A BOOLEAN, `years with the Board` IS A NUMBER, `years with the Agency` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of service the Agency must recognise` MEANS
    IF `employed in the Board's national metrology centre immediately before 1 January 2008`
    THEN `years with the Board` PLUS `years with the Agency`
    ELSE `years with the Agency`

§§ `5 and Schedule -- members`

-- s 5(1): the Agency consists of "(a) a Chairperson; and (b) not less than 8 and not more than 20 other members".
-- Schedule para 3(1): "The Minister may appoint not more than 2 members to be Deputy Chairpersons".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members is within section 5` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 8 AND `other members` AT MOST 20

GIVEN `deputies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of Deputy Chairpersons is allowed` IF
    `deputies` AT MOST 2

-- Schedule para 11: no person may be appointed or continue as a member if he or she "(a) has a mental disorder and is incapable
-- of managing himself or herself, or his or her affairs; (b) is an undischarged bankrupt or has made any arrangement or
-- composition with his or her creditors; or (c) is convicted of an offence involving dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude and has
-- not received a free pardon." Limb (b)'s "arrangement or composition" carries no time limit in the text.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `has a mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is incapable of managing self or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has ever made an arrangement or composition with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified` IF
        (`the candidate`'s `has a mental disorder` AND `the candidate`'s `is incapable of managing self or affairs`)
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `has ever made an arrangement or composition with creditors`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `is convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `has received a free pardon`))

-- Schedule para 9: the office is vacated if the member "(a) has been absent, without leave of the Agency, from 3 consecutive
-- meetings of the Agency; or (b) becomes in any manner disqualified from membership of the Agency."
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER, `disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacated` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3 OR `disqualified`

§§ `Schedule para 13 -- meetings`

-- para 13(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the Agency is the higher of the following: (a) one-third of the total number of
-- members; (b) 3 members." (s 2: "member" includes the Chairperson.) One-third may be a fraction; the test below compares
-- three times those present with the total rather than rounding.
GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quorum` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`total members` DIVIDED BY 3) 3

GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `total members` AND `present` AT LEAST 3

-- para 13(3): "A decision ... is to be adopted by a simple majority of the members present and voting except that in the case of
-- an equality of votes the Chairperson or member presiding has a casting vote in addition to his or her original vote."
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the presiding member casts for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is adopted` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the presiding member casts for`)

-- para 13(6): "Where not less than 4 members of the Agency request the Chairperson by written notice signed by them to convene a
-- meeting ... the Chairperson must, within 7 days from the receipt of the notice, convene a meeting for that purpose."
GIVEN `members who signed` IS A NUMBER, `by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chairperson must convene a meeting` IF
    `members who signed` AT LEAST 4 AND `by written notice`

GIVEN `day the notice was received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to convene` MEANS
    `day the notice was received` PLUS 7
